  "body": "## What changed\n\nLathe Facing faced only the part model, so a bar at its finished length under a longer stock reported \"nothing to face\". Turning a bar to length from a facing allowance declared in the stock was not expressible.\n\n- `camcraft_motion::turning::facing` takes the setup's stock (`Option<&[Triangle]>`) beside the part. The spindle axis is still fitted to the part alone; the stock is read in that frame, and its end and radius widen the ladder's top, every rung's band (the reach sweep runs over part + stock triangles) and the rapids radius.\n- The app's Facing arm passes the setup's stock facets.\n- \"nothing to face\" now names both the part and its stock.\n- The no-gouge construction (ball tangent to the facing plane) is untouched: stock only adds rungs above the part and pushes pass starts/rapids further out.\n- Decision recorded in `RECOMMENDED.md` (#122).\n\n## Readings\n\n- `golden/nc/fanuc-lathe/facing.nc`: each pass now starts at Ø13.6 (bar stock r6 + 0.8 nose) instead of Ø11.6 (r5 neck + nose, which was inside the raw r6 bar). Rapids (Ø14.6) and every other line unchanged.\n- `lathe_spindle_law::a_plumb_bar_on_the_origin_or_under_a_moved_work_offset_posts_the_same_program`: the fixture now moves its box stock with the bar and G54 (a blank left behind is a different job now that facing reads it).\n\n## Not covered\n\nPosting the whole face-then-drill lathe program is still refused by the footprint rapid law on the facing's inward rapids - #159 (same refusal on main, rides #103 / PR #135). The new pin asserts the facing and the drill verdicts and can gain the post line when #159 lands.\n\n## Gate (own worktree build, rebased on 8b3163d)\n\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-motion --tests`: all green except `swarf_pose_continuity` x2 - identical failure on main (pre-existing).\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --tests`: all green except `drilling_axial::a_drill_where_the_model_has_no_hole_is_convicted` and `lathe_field_sim::profile_rough_and_finish_simulate_with_meridian_parity` - identical failures on main (pre-existing). `lathe_post` and `lathe_spindle_law` green after the two test updates above.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `turning_face::a_stock_allowance_above_the_finished_part_is_faced_off`\n- `drill_prior::a_stock_facing_allowance_is_faced_and_the_drill_after_it_stands`\n- `drill_prior::a_finished_part_with_no_stock_allowance_has_nothing_to_face`\n\nChangelog: Lathe Facing faces the stock's allowance down to the part's end instead of reporting nothing to face\n\nOutside contributor PR (fork).\n\nFixes #122\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
